::MCR_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.8
Question:
A shipping rule charges $6 for packages up to 2 pounds and $10 for packages over 2 pounds up to 5 pounds. What is the cost for a 2-pound package?
{
=A. $6#Correct. Up to 2 pounds includes exactly 2 pounds.
~B. $8#This amount is not one of the stated rules.
~C. $10#This rule is for packages over 2 pounds, not exactly 2 pounds.
~D. $16#This adds both rules instead of choosing the correct interval.
}
::MCR_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q02::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.8
Question:
Using the same shipping rule, what is the cost for a 3-pound package?
{
~A. $6#This is the rule for packages up to 2 pounds.
=B. $10#Correct. 3 pounds is over 2 and up to 5, so the cost is $10.
~C. $3#This uses the weight as the cost.
~D. $16#This adds both charges instead of choosing the correct interval.
}
::MCR_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q03::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.8
Question:
What is a boundary in a piecewise model?
{
~A. The output only#A boundary is an input value, not just an output.
~B. A graph title#A title does not determine where the rule changes.
=C. The input value where the rule changes#Correct. A boundary is where the model switches from one rule to another.
~D. The largest possible answer#The boundary may or may not be the largest value.
}
::MCR_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q04::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.8
Question:
Which phrase means the endpoint is included?
{
~A. Less than#Less than does not include the endpoint.
~B. Greater than#Greater than does not include the endpoint.
~C. Over#Over means greater than, so it does not include the endpoint.
=D. Up to and including#Correct. Including means the boundary value belongs in the interval.
}
::MCR_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q05::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.8
Question:
A parking garage charges $5 for the first hour and $3 for each additional hour. Why is this piecewise?
{
~A. The cost never changes#The cost does change when time changes.
=B. The rule changes after the first hour#Correct. A different rule applies after the first hour.
~C. The graph must be curved#Piecewise graphs are not always curved.
~D. There is no input#The input is time parked.
}